WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.296
This is Haulcast.

2
00:00:02.346 --> 00:00:05.608
It helps a truck driver choose the safest of three routes,

3
00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:08.584
weighing weather, load and travel time.

4
00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:11.484
Search the origin and destination, pick a departure,

5
00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:12.972
and enter the load.

6
00:00:13.022 --> 00:00:15.772
The hint shows which wind rules apply.

7
00:00:15.822 --> 00:00:17.997
Then choose a checkpoint every ten,

8
00:00:18.047 --> 00:00:20.334
twenty-five or fifty miles.

9
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.245
Haulcast finds three truck routes, and reads the forecast at each checkpoint

10
00:00:25.295 --> 00:00:27.554
, for the hour the truck will reach it.

11
00:00:27.604 --> 00:00:31.129
Wind, rain and snow are scored with the brief's thresholds,

12
00:00:31.179 --> 00:00:33.904
and heavy loads tighten the wind limits.

13
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.793
The decision comes first.

14
00:00:35.843 --> 00:00:38.531
Routes rank by No Travel miles, then Severe,

15
00:00:38.581 --> 00:00:41.581
then High, then average risk, then time.

16
00:00:41.631 --> 00:00:46.800
Route C crosses No Travel wind, so Route B wins on average risk.

17
00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.486
Each strip is the road, colored by risk.

18
00:00:49.536 --> 00:00:51.473
Hover a stretch, and its checkpoint lights up,

19
00:00:51.523 --> 00:00:53.848
with the arrival time, wind, gusts,

20
00:00:53.898 --> 00:00:55.200
rain and snow.

21
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.668
The Checkpoints tab lists every stop.

22
00:00:57.718 --> 00:00:59.681
Click one to fly there.

23
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.871
Press Play, and the truck drives the route while the forty-eight hour

24
00:01:02.921 --> 00:01:04.521
heatmap moves with it.

25
00:01:04.571 --> 00:01:07.534
Scrub to any hour, or switch between risk,

26
00:01:07.584 --> 00:01:09.700
wind, rain and snow.

27
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.272
At thirty thousand pounds, that stretch drops to Severe.

28
00:01:13.322 --> 00:01:16.022
And on a calm trip, like Chicago to Denver,

29
00:01:16.072 --> 00:01:18.297
the fastest route wins.

30
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.017
On a phone, the forecast sits on top,

31
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:23.850
and the sheet keeps the recommendation in view.

32
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.788
Every plan is a shareable link.

33
00:01:25.838 --> 00:01:27.463
That's Haulcast.
